{"id": "EUVD-2026-103759", "enisaUuid": "2d300802-01c6-3253-9db8-6d44a2950ed6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: Fix runtime PM leak in amdgpu_debugfs_test_ib_show()\n\namdgpu_debugfs_test_ib_show() resumes the device with\npm_runtime_get_sync() before taking the reset domain semaphore with\ndown_write_killable().  If the write lock acquisition is interrupted,\nthe function returns without calling pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(),\nleaking the runtime PM reference acquired for the device and keeping\nthe GPU awake.\n\nDrop the runtime PM reference on the interrupted down_write_killable()\nerror path before returning.\n\n(cherry picked from commit ec30a576c2d4c0364549e6c04218f50704ef56c8)", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc5606ac91642d0f184b83ab833148c457c3c331", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c1a643942caae938ea84df2648a9b0c136e09be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e016347fb1829489e062ea51a98a51f48b1d582d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c28e74395ab09922bbf5be42bc5a6ed1ba4f3c37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2556dd3a36beb3a11041ef01b5e9762e2157909f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b86ab1bd6673c525adda88819d7658ba9e784ec"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98519", "GHSA-6qmp-28g8-3p6v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22feff93-e5cf-3f35-b439-3c2b78db5b72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "244be298-8f35-367b-9f0e-9b16c6a54944", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6049db43d6dd9cbb9d7f897839d15b0bc600e23c <e016347fb1829489e062ea51a98a51f48b1d582d"}, {"id": "47b23160-5f63-3185-a454-473bd6a66f17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "632f9ead-5f6e-3ad7-9a08-3287c692713d", "product": {"name": "Linu